  "question": {
    "text": "An observer finds that the angular elevation of a tower is <math><mi>θ</mi><mo>.</mo></math> On advancing <math><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>m</mi></math> towards the tower, the elevation is <math><msup><mrow><mn>45</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> and on advancing <math><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;further more towards the tower, the elevation is <math><msup><mrow><mn>90</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The height of the tower is (assume the height of observer is negligible and observer lies on the same level as the foot of the tower)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Aomdm",
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>m</mi></math>",
